<title>ISRAEL: Israel Discount Bank to sell Canadian unit.</title>
<headline>Israel Discount Bank to sell Canadian unit.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel Discount Bank said on Monday that it was selling its Canadian subsidiary to Republic National Bank of New York for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>Israel Discount of Canada has one branch in Toronto and had assets of 95 million Canadian dollars at the end of October, a Discount spokeswoman said. Discount, Israel's third-largest bank, said the transaction would be completed after regulatory approvals.</p>
<p>&quot;Our bank in Canada hasn't lost money over the years, but its financial situation didn't justify holding on to it and strengthening it,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
